    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju saw wheat grow in a field, a mill make flour and a shop sell bread.\n\"All three are linked,\" said his teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "primary sector",
     "secondary sector",
     "tertiary sector"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The primary sector takes things from nature: farming, fishing, mining. The secondary sector makes things from them: flour mills, factories. The tertiary sector gives services: teaching, banking, transport and shops.\nThe sectors depend on each other. Farmers supply wheat to mills, mills supply flour to bakers and shops sell bread.\nA growing economy has more people in secondary and tertiary work."
    }
